# Files Semgrep should not gate this repository's CI on.
#
# labs/week*/ and project/starter-app/ are intentionally vulnerable teaching
# material: SQL injection, command injection, `gets()`, JWT `alg: none`, planted
# secrets, an unhardened Dockerfile students are asked to fix. Gating CI on them
# keeps the build red forever and the signal worthless. Students still see those
# findings by running the scanners inside the lab (labs/week15-devsecops-pipeline
# is the pipeline they watch fail on purpose).
#
# Everything else IS still gated — notably labs/live-quiz (the real quiz platform)
# and tools/, so a genuine finding in code we actually run still fails the build.
labs/week*/
project/starter-app/
# interactive attacker/dev shell (gdb + ptrace); root is the point, never exposed
labs/toolbox/

# Never committed (git-ignored), but keeps local runs equal to CI
instructor/

# NOTE: supplying this file replaces Semgrep's built-in ignore list, so the usual
# defaults have to be restated here — otherwise test suites and vendored code get
# scanned and gate the build (e.g. `app.config["TESTING"] = True` in pytest files).
:include .gitignore
tests/
test/
*_test.py
test_*.py

# Vendored third-party assets (self-hosted socket.io client)
*.min.js

# Standard noise
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
dist/
build/
